   "source": [
    "# Fine-tuning de Florence-2 para Generación de Captions\n",
    "\n",
    "Este notebook realiza el fine-tuning del modelo **Florence-2** de Microsoft para la tarea de generación automática de captions de imágenes.\n",
    "\n",
    "El proceso sigue estos pasos:\n",
    "1. Configuración del entorno y GPU\n",
    "2. Descarga del dataset desde HuggingFace\n",
    "3. Clonación del repositorio de entrenamiento\n",
    "4. Instalación de dependencias\n",
    "5. Entrenamiento del modelo con LoRA\n",
    "6. Guardado del modelo en Google Drive\n",
    "\n",
    "**Modelo:** `microsoft/Florence-2-base-ft`  \n",
    "**Técnica:** LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) — permite fine-tuning eficiente con pocos recursos  \n",
    "**Dataset:** `LolaCPP/dataset_captioning_TFG`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Verificar GPU disponible\n",
    "\n",
    "Antes de empezar, verificamos que Colab nos ha asignado una GPU. Ve a **Entorno de ejecución > Cambiar tipo de entorno de ejecución > T4 GPU**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    gpu = torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)\n",
    "    mem = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ GPU disponible: {gpu}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   Memoria total: {mem:.1f} GB\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"❌ No hay GPU disponible. Ve a Entorno de ejecución > Cambiar tipo de entorno de ejecución > T4 GPU\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Montar Google Drive\n",
    "\n",
    "Montamos Google Drive para guardar los checkpoints del modelo. Así, si la sesión de Colab se interrumpe, no perdemos el progreso."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "CHECKPOINTS_DIR = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/TFG/checkpoints_florence2\"\n",
    "os.makedirs(CHECKPOINTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Checkpoints se guardarán en: {CHECKPOINTS_DIR}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Clonar el repositorio\n",
    "\n",
    "Clonamos la versión propia del proyecto, que incluye los arreglos de compatibilidad necesarios para que Florence-2 funcione correctamente con las versiones actuales de las librerías."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%cd /content\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/LolaCPP/prueba3.git caption-train\n",
    "%cd caption-train\n",
    "!git log --oneline -5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Instalar dependencias\n",
    "\n",
    "Instalamos todas las dependencias del proyecto. El proyecto usa `uv` como gestor de paquetes, pero en Colab usaremos `pip` directamente para mayor compatibilidad."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q transformers accelerate peft datasets timm einops\n",
    "!pip install -q prodigyplus\n",
    "!pip install -e . -q\n",
    "print(\"✅ Dependencias instaladas\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Descargar el dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "Descargamos el dataset desde HuggingFace (`LolaCPP/dataset_captioning_TFG`) y lo convertimos al formato imagen + archivo `.txt` de caption que espera el pipeline de entrenamiento."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from datasets import load_dataset\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "ds = load_dataset(\"LolaCPP/dataset_captioning_TFG\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if isinstance(ds, dict) and \"train\" in ds:\n",
    "    ds = ds[\"train\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset cargado: {len(ds)} ejemplos\")\n",
    "print(f\"Columnas: {ds.column_names}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mostrar un ejemplo\n",
    "example = ds[0]\n",
    "print(f\"\\nEjemplo de caption: {str(list(example.values())[1])[:200]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "output_dir = Path(\"./data/dataset_captioning_TFG\")\n",
    "output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, example in enumerate(ds):\n",
    "    image = example[\"image\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    if \"text\" in example:\n",
    "        caption = example[\"text\"]\n",
    "    elif \"caption\" in example:\n",
    "        caption = example[\"caption\"]\n",
    "    elif \"captions\" in example:\n",
    "        caption = example[\"captions\"]\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"No encuentro columna de caption. Columnas: {ds.column_names}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    image_path = output_dir / f\"{i:06d}.jpg\"\n",
    "    caption_path = output_dir / f\"{i:06d}.txt\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    image.save(image_path)\n",
    "    caption_path.write_text(str(caption), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    if i % 100 == 0:\n",
    "        print(f\"  {i}/{len(ds)} imágenes exportadas...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✅ {len(ds)} imágenes exportadas a {output_dir}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Aplicar parche de compatibilidad a Florence-2\n",
    "\n",
    "La versión de Florence-2 descargada de HuggingFace tiene un desajuste en la clase `Florence2Seq2SeqLMOutput`: su método `forward()` devuelve campos (`loss`, `logits`, `image_hidden_states`) que no están declarados en la clase. Aplicamos un parche directo al archivo cacheado para añadir esos campos."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import glob\n",
    "\n",
    "# Encontrar el archivo del modelo cacheado\n",
    "pattern = \"/root/.cache/huggingface/modules/transformers_modules/microsoft/Florence-2-base-ft/*/modeling_florence2.py\"\n",
    "matches = glob.glob(pattern)\n",
    "\n",
    "if not matches:\n",
    "    # Forzar descarga para que aparezca en caché\n",
    "    from transformers import AutoProcessor\n",
    "    AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(\"microsoft/Florence-2-base-ft\", trust_remote_code=True)\n",
    "    matches = glob.glob(pattern)\n",
    "\n",
    "if matches:\n",
    "    model_file = matches[0]\n",
    "    print(f\"Archivo encontrado: {model_file}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    with open(model_file, \"r\") as f:\n",
    "        content = f.read()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Aplicar parche: añadir loss, logits e image_hidden_states a Florence2Seq2SeqLMOutput\n",
    "    old = \"    last_hidden_state: torch.FloatTensor = None\"\n",
    "    new = \"\"\"    loss: Optional[torch.FloatTensor] = None\n",
    "    logits: Optional[torch.FloatTensor] = None\n",
    "    last_hidden_state: torch.FloatTensor = None\n",
    "    image_hidden_states: Optional[Tuple[torch.FloatTensor, ...]] = None\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    if old in content and \"loss: Optional[torch.FloatTensor]\" not in content:\n",
    "        content = content.replace(old, new)\n",
    "        with open(model_file, \"w\") as f:\n",
    "            f.write(content)\n",
    "        print(\"✅ Parche aplicado correctamente\")\n",
    "    elif \"loss: Optional[torch.FloatTensor]\" in content:\n",
    "        print(\"✅ El parche ya estaba aplicado\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"⚠️ No se encontró el patrón esperado. Revisa el archivo manualmente.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"⚠️ No se encontró el archivo del modelo. Se aplicará tras la primera carga.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Configuración del entrenamiento\n",
    "\n",
    "Definimos los hiperparámetros principales. Con LoRA solo se entrenan ~1.6M parámetros de los 272M totales del modelo (~0.6%), lo que hace el entrenamiento mucho más eficiente en memoria y tiempo.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Parámetro | Valor | Descripción |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `MODEL_ID` | Florence-2-base-ft | Modelo base preentrenado |\n",
    "| `EPOCHS` | 5 | Pasadas completas sobre el dataset |\n",
    "| `BATCH_SIZE` | 4 | Imágenes por paso de entrenamiento |\n",
    "| `LEARNING_RATE` | 1e-5 | Velocidad de aprendizaje |\n",
    "| `LORA_RANK` | 8 | Rango de las matrices LoRA |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Configuración ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "MODEL_ID       = \"microsoft/Florence-2-base-ft\"\n",
    "DATASET_DIR    = \"./data/dataset_captioning_TFG\"\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR     = CHECKPOINTS_DIR   # guardado directo en Drive\n",
    "EPOCHS         = 5\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE     = 4\n",
    "LEARNING_RATE  = 1e-5\n",
    "LORA_RANK      = 8\n",
    "LORA_ALPHA     = 8\n",
    "# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Configuración del entrenamiento:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Modelo:          {MODEL_ID}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Dataset:         {DATASET_DIR}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Checkpoints:     {OUTPUT_DIR}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Épocas:          {EPOCHS}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Batch size:      {BATCH_SIZE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Learning rate:   {LEARNING_RATE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  LoRA rank:       {LORA_RANK}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Entrenamiento\n",
    "\n",
    "Lanzamos el script de entrenamiento. El proceso:\n",
    "- Carga Florence-2 con adaptadores LoRA\n",
    "- Entrena solo los parámetros LoRA (~1.6M)\n",
    "- Guarda checkpoints en Google Drive al finalizar\n",
    "\n",
    "Con una GPU T4 y batch_size=4, cada época tarda aproximadamente **10-15 minutos**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python scripts/training/train_florence.py \\\n",
    "    --dataset {DATASET_DIR} \\\n",
    "    --output_dir {OUTPUT_DIR} \\\n",
    "    --model_id {MODEL_ID} \\\n",
    "    --learning_rate {LEARNING_RATE} \\\n",
    "    --batch_size {BATCH_SIZE} \\\n",
    "    --epochs {EPOCHS} \\\n",
    "    --rank {LORA_RANK} \\\n",
    "    --alpha {LORA_ALPHA} \\\n",
    "    --gradient_checkpointing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Verificar checkpoints guardados"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "files = list(Path(OUTPUT_DIR).rglob(\"*\"))\n",
    "if files:\n",
    "    print(f\"✅ Checkpoints guardados en {OUTPUT_DIR}:\")\n",
    "    for f in sorted(files):\n",
    "        size = os.path.getsize(f) / 1e6\n",
    "        print(f\"   {f.name} ({size:.1f} MB)\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"⚠️ No se encontraron checkpoints. Revisa si el entrenamiento terminó correctamente.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Inferencia — probar el modelo entrenado\n",
    "\n",
    "Probamos el modelo fine-tuneado generando captions para algunas imágenes del dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import AutoProcessor, AutoModelForCausalLM\n",
    "from peft import PeftModel\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import random\n",
    "\n",
    "device = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cargar modelo base + adaptadores LoRA\n",
    "print(\"Cargando modelo...\")\n",
    "processor = AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID, trust_remote_code=True)\n",
    "base_model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    MODEL_ID,\n",
    "    trust_remote_code=True,\n",
    "    torch_dtype=torch.float16,\n",
    ").to(device)\n",
    "model = PeftModel.from_pretrained(base_model, OUTPUT_DIR)\n",
    "model.eval()\n",
    "print(\"✅ Modelo cargado\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def generate_caption(image_path, model, processor, device):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Genera un caption para una imagen usando el modelo fine-tuneado.\"\"\"\n",
    "    image = Image.open(image_path).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
    "    task = \"<MORE_DETAILED_CAPTION>\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    inputs = processor(\n",
    "        text=task,\n",
    "        images=image,\n",
    "        return_tensors=\"pt\"\n",
    "    ).to(device, torch.float16)\n",
    "\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        output_ids = model.generate(\n",
    "            **inputs,\n",
    "            max_new_tokens=128,\n",
    "            num_beams=3,\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "    caption = processor.decode(output_ids[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n",
    "    return image, caption\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Probar con 3 imágenes aleatorias del dataset\n",
    "image_files = sorted(Path(DATASET_DIR).glob(\"*.jpg\"))[:3]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(image_files), figsize=(18, 6))\n",
    "for ax, image_path in zip(axes, image_files):\n",
    "    image, caption = generate_caption(image_path, model, processor, device)\n",
    "    caption_ref = image_path.with_suffix(\".txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.imshow(image)\n",
    "    ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(\n",
    "        f\"Generado:\\n{caption[:120]}...\\n\\nRef: {caption_ref[:80]}...\",\n",
    "        fontsize=8, wrap=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(f\"{OUTPUT_DIR}/ejemplos_inferencia.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print(\"✅ Ejemplos guardados en Drive\")"
   ]
  }
 ]
}"
